WEBVTT

00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:05.590
<i>We...</i>

00:00:05.590 --> 00:00:08.280
<i>can't lose at a place like this!</i>

00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:11.920
It got through!

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:14.400
Shigeno!

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:16.250
That guy... He's going for the cut-off?

00:00:16.820 --> 00:00:17.290
Over here!

00:00:17.290 --> 00:00:18.130
Okay!

00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:22.840
I can't allow you to get any more runs!

00:00:31.230 --> 00:00:34.940
<i>It was in my calculations... that shoulder.</i>

00:00:36.330 --> 00:00:39.270
<i>Not bad, my childhood friend. </i>

00:02:15.100 --> 00:02:18.120
Batting fifth: pitcher, Yamane-kun.

00:02:19.050 --> 00:02:21.840
<i>No outs, a runner on second, and it's Yamane, huh?</i>

00:02:23.650 --> 00:02:25.240
<i>This is bad.</i>

00:02:25.240 --> 00:02:27.310
<i>Even though it's still the bottom of the sixth,</i>

00:02:27.310 --> 00:02:31.270
<i>if they get their fourth run here, we'll be done for.</i>

00:02:33.430 --> 00:02:36.680
<i>I can't allow Komori to reach home no matter what.</i>

00:02:40.600 --> 00:02:41.230
It's a sacrifice bunt!

00:02:43.940 --> 00:02:44.730
A push bunt!?

00:02:49.760 --> 00:02:51.610
All right! All safe!

00:02:53.320 --> 00:02:53.830
Damn!

00:02:55.590 --> 00:02:57.250
F-Fuji!

00:02:57.690 --> 00:02:58.960
Second!

00:03:01.390 --> 00:03:02.420
What!?

00:03:03.490 --> 00:03:04.630
Y-You!

00:03:06.680 --> 00:03:07.790
W-Wait!

00:03:07.790 --> 00:03:09.050
Don't chase him, Fuji!

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:18.400
All right, I did it!

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:20.550
I tagged a runner out!

00:03:27.030 --> 00:03:29.180
All right! Yeah!

00:03:29.180 --> 00:03:31.200
All right! The fourth run!

00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:34.700
Nice, Yamane! He went along with the trick, just as we thought!

00:03:45.800 --> 00:03:47.050
<i>We won.</i>

00:03:57.560 --> 00:03:59.070
Top of the eighth inning:

00:03:59.070 --> 00:04:01.510
leading off for Seishuu High School... 

00:04:01.510 --> 00:04:04.480
Batting first: pitcher, Shimizu-kun.

00:04:06.110 --> 00:04:08.240
<i>All three were struck out in the seventh inning...</i>

00:04:09.500 --> 00:04:11.150
<i>This inning's going to determine who wins, isn't it?</i>

00:04:11.840 --> 00:04:14.110
<i>This is seriously our last chance.</i>

00:04:14.110 --> 00:04:15.570
<i>I'm counting on you...</i>

00:04:15.570 --> 00:04:17.870
<i>Please let me get out there somehow!</i>

00:04:21.580 --> 00:04:22.370
Strike!

00:04:33.310 --> 00:04:35.970
Is Shimizu-kun all right?

00:04:35.970 --> 00:04:39.090
He's already thrown about 120 pitches since the beginning...

00:04:39.090 --> 00:04:40.180
That's true...

00:04:40.870 --> 00:04:41.950
<i>Taiga...</i>

00:04:43.820 --> 00:04:46.190
We've done well.

00:04:46.930 --> 00:04:51.790
In our first tournament, with such little fighting capability, we've done well.

00:04:52.480 --> 00:04:54.010
I don't have any more regrets.

00:04:54.720 --> 00:04:58.160
In my last year of high school, I was able to make some good memories.

00:05:03.340 --> 00:05:04.750
Damn!

00:05:08.080 --> 00:05:09.340
<i>Damn...</i>

00:05:09.340 --> 00:05:10.590
<i>I can't let it end.</i>

00:05:10.590 --> 00:05:12.220
<i>If I lose like this,</i>

00:05:12.220 --> 00:05:17.140
<i>I'll only be able to remember... that I got hit in this tournament!</i>

00:05:21.050 --> 00:05:22.890
Safe! Safe!

00:05:24.230 --> 00:05:25.140
All right!

00:05:25.650 --> 00:05:26.810
We got a runner on base!

00:05:35.770 --> 00:05:36.920
Tashiro.

00:05:39.540 --> 00:05:42.660
It's too early to make it a memory.

00:05:45.820 --> 00:05:48.580
Batting second: third baseman, Uchiyama-kun.

00:05:48.580 --> 00:05:51.090
All right! Keep it up, Uchiyama!

00:05:53.950 --> 00:05:56.770
<i>It's all right. It's a four-run difference.</i>

00:05:56.770 --> 00:05:59.760
<i>If we continue what we've been doing, there's nothing to be afraid of.</i>

00:06:02.200 --> 00:06:03.180
Ball!

00:06:03.780 --> 00:06:04.850
All right!

00:06:05.890 --> 00:06:07.880
<i>Who cares?</i>

00:06:07.880 --> 00:06:10.400
<i>Just hurry up and end this already.</i>

00:06:10.400 --> 00:06:13.610
<i>We're going to lose because of me anyway.</i>

00:06:15.040 --> 00:06:15.900
Ball!

00:06:20.490 --> 00:06:23.320
<i>The breaking balls aren't going to the places I want them to anymore.</i>

00:06:23.980 --> 00:06:26.620
<i>Yamane-kun's getting pretty tired, huh?</i>

00:06:29.560 --> 00:06:30.750
<i>Too easy! It's right down the middle!</i>

00:06:34.630 --> 00:06:35.620
All right!

00:06:35.620 --> 00:06:37.380
No outs, and runners on first and second!

00:06:39.710 --> 00:06:41.360
K-Komori!

00:06:42.390 --> 00:06:43.430
T-Time!

00:06:49.270 --> 00:06:50.560
<i>All right.</i>

00:06:50.560 --> 00:06:53.110
<i>Now they won't be able to walk Tashiro anymore.</i>

00:06:53.110 --> 00:06:55.310
<i>The wind's finally blowing in our direction!</i>

00:07:00.260 --> 00:07:02.340
I guess we'll just have to face him.

00:07:02.340 --> 00:07:05.740
If we allow this batter to walk, we'll bring it around to Honda-kun.

00:07:06.280 --> 00:07:07.480
It's all right.

00:07:07.480 --> 00:07:11.960
The power has dropped, but even if he hits a home run, we'll still be leading by one run.

00:07:12.940 --> 00:07:14.560
Let's do our best!

00:07:14.560 --> 00:07:15.420
Yeah.

00:07:16.220 --> 00:07:19.420
Batting third: catcher, Tashiro-kun.

00:07:20.090 --> 00:07:23.250
<i>That guy... He said it so clearly.</i>

00:07:24.340 --> 00:07:25.350
Play!

00:07:27.100 --> 00:07:30.600
<i>I... won't become depressed because of this!</i>

00:07:32.310 --> 00:07:33.560
Strike!

00:07:36.570 --> 00:07:37.480
Nice ball!

00:07:42.070 --> 00:07:44.190
<i>He's starting to pitch well again.</i>

00:07:44.190 --> 00:07:45.750
<i>As expected of Komori.</i>

00:07:45.750 --> 00:07:48.700
<i>He must have said something to encourage Yamane.</i>

00:07:49.940 --> 00:07:51.380
<i>They're finally facing me, huh? </i>

00:07:52.230 --> 00:07:53.170
<i>I've been waiting for this!</i>

00:07:57.070 --> 00:08:02.220
<i>He's a dangerous hitter, but today... this is his first real time batting.</i>

00:08:03.200 --> 00:08:06.680
<i>If he's not used to the way Yamane-kun's balls move...</i>

00:08:07.110 --> 00:08:08.850
<i>Bring it together, Tashiro!</i>

00:08:09.320 --> 00:08:11.100
<i>There's a huge chance we'll win!</i>

00:08:17.150 --> 00:08:18.070
Out!

00:08:19.840 --> 00:08:20.840
Out!

00:08:20.840 --> 00:08:21.860
All right!

00:08:22.240 --> 00:08:23.450
We did it!

00:08:23.450 --> 00:08:24.320
Double play!

00:08:33.870 --> 00:08:35.370
Our chance...

00:08:35.370 --> 00:08:39.130
In an instant... two outs and a runner on third.

00:08:42.440 --> 00:08:43.630
I-I'm sorry...

00:08:46.340 --> 00:08:48.760
It's okay. Don't worry about it!

00:08:51.590 --> 00:08:54.780
Batting fourth: second baseman, Fuji-kun.

00:08:59.180 --> 00:09:02.630
<i>I'm glad that Tashiro batted poorly.</i>

00:09:02.630 --> 00:09:05.850
<i>Now I don't have to bear all the blame alone. </i>

00:09:08.680 --> 00:09:09.740
Strike!

00:09:19.420 --> 00:09:23.710
<i>In the end, it's over so quickly: my high school baseball.</i>

00:09:27.910 --> 00:09:29.180
Idiot!

00:09:29.180 --> 00:09:31.730
How much longer are you going to be depressed for, Fuji!?

00:09:31.730 --> 00:09:33.210
It's fine if it's just one run!

00:09:33.210 --> 00:09:35.980
Why don't you at least try to get a run!?

00:09:36.680 --> 00:09:40.120
If this goes on, this'll be your last time to bat!

00:09:40.120 --> 00:09:43.590
Don't let it end with your half-hearted play!

00:09:49.140 --> 00:09:50.900
<i>T-That's right...</i>

00:09:50.900 --> 00:09:55.160
<i>I... have been thinking too much about my mistakes in the previous innings. </i>

00:09:57.670 --> 00:10:01.170
<i>Tashiro was walked in front of me so many times...</i>

00:10:04.220 --> 00:10:05.460
<i>I made errors...</i>

00:10:06.670 --> 00:10:10.440
<i>And I even allowed another run because of my fatal mistake.</i>

00:10:15.200 --> 00:10:15.980
<i>If that's the case,</i>

00:10:18.150 --> 00:10:20.440
<i>I can only get it back...</i>

00:10:21.110 --> 00:10:22.690
<i>with my bat!</i>

00:10:28.820 --> 00:10:33.790
This is a free fansub.

00:10:28.820 --> 00:10:33.790
Not for sale or rent.

00:10:41.360 --> 00:10:42.250
Yamane-kun, above you!

00:10:43.180 --> 00:10:44.100
What?

00:10:49.380 --> 00:10:49.840
Safe!

00:10:55.290 --> 00:10:57.980
At least it won't be a shutout now.

00:10:57.980 --> 00:10:59.500
All right!

00:10:59.500 --> 00:11:01.480
We finally got one run back!

00:11:02.090 --> 00:11:04.450
Fuji! Nice batting!

00:11:06.650 --> 00:11:11.460
If it hadn't made an irregular bounce off the mound, Yamane would've gotten it.

00:11:12.880 --> 00:11:17.330
Not yet... The goddess of victory hasn't left our side yet!

00:11:18.170 --> 00:11:19.600
All right!

00:11:19.600 --> 00:11:22.290
Batting fifth: shortstop, Hattori-kun.

00:11:23.170 --> 00:11:24.590
<i>No problem.</i>

00:11:24.590 --> 00:11:27.240
<i>It's still a three-run difference with two outs.</i>

00:11:27.240 --> 00:11:29.680
<i>If we get this batter out...</i>

00:11:51.580 --> 00:11:52.390
Play!

00:11:53.490 --> 00:11:55.480
Hattori! Go!

00:11:55.480 --> 00:11:57.700
Do whatever you can! Let Shigeno get out there!

00:12:01.600 --> 00:12:02.500
Ball!

00:12:03.020 --> 00:12:07.500
No, even if Hattori gets out there, won't Shigeno be walked?

00:12:08.450 --> 00:12:12.260
Last time, it was two outs, with runners on first and second, and he was walked.

00:12:12.260 --> 00:12:16.940
This time for sure, if they throw to a place where his bat can't hit it...

00:12:16.940 --> 00:12:19.510
Even if it gets to Shigeno, there's no point.

00:12:22.230 --> 00:12:23.180
Ball!

00:12:23.180 --> 00:12:24.480
Ball two.

00:12:25.260 --> 00:12:26.150
T-Time!

00:12:28.620 --> 00:12:30.150
What's wrong, Yamane-kun?

00:12:30.780 --> 00:12:35.920
If you worry about Honda-kun, who's up next, and walk this batter, there's no point!

00:12:35.920 --> 00:12:38.780
Even if it gets around to him, we're going to walk Honda-kun,

00:12:38.780 --> 00:12:40.350
so you can just ignore him!

00:12:40.350 --> 00:12:43.620
Anyways, if we don't end it here, the risk will be greater.

00:12:44.330 --> 00:12:47.510
Even if the ball becomes easier to hit, we have to battle it out right now. 

00:12:51.750 --> 00:12:53.260
I'm not going to ignore him.

00:12:55.850 --> 00:12:57.430
Did you say something?

00:12:58.710 --> 00:13:00.480
You! Are you ready yet?

00:13:01.090 --> 00:13:02.430
Yes! I'm sorry!

00:13:11.110 --> 00:13:12.360
Play!

00:13:13.950 --> 00:13:15.170
<i>What was that?</i>

00:13:15.170 --> 00:13:17.600
<i>I heard him say he wasn't going to ignore him but...</i>

00:13:21.170 --> 00:13:23.410
Ball! Ball three.

00:13:29.300 --> 00:13:30.540
<i>D-Don't tell me...!</i>

00:13:30.900 --> 00:13:33.350
I-I'm sorry... Time!

00:13:33.350 --> 00:13:34.510
Again?

00:13:36.310 --> 00:13:39.760
After getting hit by the fourth batter, his pitching is completely different!

00:13:45.820 --> 00:13:46.600
You did it on purpose...

00:13:47.360 --> 00:13:49.480
In order to go up against Honda-kun,

00:13:49.480 --> 00:13:52.520
you're going to purposely allow this batter to walk, aren't you!?

00:13:53.180 --> 00:13:54.410
Yeah.

00:13:54.410 --> 00:13:56.760
That's why I said I wasn't going to ignore him!

00:13:58.710 --> 00:13:59.810
You can't do that!

00:13:59.810 --> 00:14:01.210
You definitely can't do that!

00:14:01.210 --> 00:14:04.170
If Honda-kun hits a home run, we're tied!

00:14:04.170 --> 00:14:05.030
That's-

00:14:05.030 --> 00:14:06.240
I won't let him hit it!

00:14:08.540 --> 00:14:12.920
Komori, I understand your feelings and the team's strategy!

00:14:13.930 --> 00:14:15.340
I don't want to lose either...

00:14:16.180 --> 00:14:18.560
or betray everyone's hopes.

00:14:19.830 --> 00:14:20.850
But, you know...

00:14:21.750 --> 00:14:24.810
I want to have a proper battle against him!

00:14:32.600 --> 00:14:38.450
During middle school, when I broke my elbow and gave up on myself, he saved me.

00:14:40.020 --> 00:14:43.780
And then, using himself as an example, he taught me, 

00:14:44.790 --> 00:14:48.210
that I could still play baseball by switching my dominant arm.

00:14:51.950 --> 00:14:54.280
He's not just a nostalgic old friend.

00:14:55.130 --> 00:14:58.180
Because he was there, I'm here today!

00:15:01.250 --> 00:15:03.020
I won't let him hit it!

00:15:03.020 --> 00:15:05.810
I'm going to show him that I've grown!

00:15:06.990 --> 00:15:12.020
That is, as a player, the greatest thank you!

00:15:20.400 --> 00:15:22.070
H-Hey!

00:15:22.680 --> 00:15:23.370
<i>What!?</i>

00:15:23.980 --> 00:15:26.330
They're walking Hattori!?

00:15:34.460 --> 00:15:36.750
Ball! Four balls.

00:15:38.120 --> 00:15:40.720
Batting sixth: first baseman, Shigeno-kun.

00:15:41.590 --> 00:15:43.180
<i>It's a battle, Honda!</i>

00:15:48.300 --> 00:15:50.980
<i>W-Why, Komori?</i>

00:15:50.980 --> 00:15:52.900
<i>Why would you purposely walk the fifth batter,</i>

00:15:53.480 --> 00:15:55.950
<i>and choose a battle with the sixth batter?</i>

00:15:57.230 --> 00:16:00.720
<i>Didn't you say that if we could take care of the third batter and this batter,</i>

00:16:00.720 --> 00:16:02.360
<i>we could defeat Seishuu?</i>

00:16:02.360 --> 00:16:03.160
Play!

00:16:04.100 --> 00:16:06.620
<i>I'm sorry, Coach.</i>

00:16:07.440 --> 00:16:11.790
<i>But it's not like I was swept away by feelings and am throwing away our chance to win.</i>

00:16:19.990 --> 00:16:21.970
<i>If it's Yamane-kun now,</i>

00:16:21.970 --> 00:16:23.220
<i>I'm sure...</i>

00:16:23.220 --> 00:16:24.800
<i>he'll be able to strike Honda-kun out!</i>

00:16:30.270 --> 00:16:31.230
Strike!

00:16:33.280 --> 00:16:34.600
T-They're facing him!

00:16:42.860 --> 00:16:44.240
<i>It's not half bad...</i>

00:16:45.130 --> 00:16:47.540
<i>How hard you've worked...</i>

00:16:47.540 --> 00:16:51.250
<i>Since I've switched from throwing with my right to throwing with my left, just like you have,</i>

00:16:51.250 --> 00:16:52.910
<i>I understand that the best.</i>

00:16:54.620 --> 00:16:56.580
<i>This is the best!</i>

00:16:57.230 --> 00:17:01.840
<i>Because I can have a proper fight with a man like you!</i>

00:17:02.750 --> 00:17:04.010
Strike!

00:17:04.430 --> 00:17:05.830
T-They've got him cornered!

00:17:05.830 --> 00:17:06.650
Damn.

00:17:06.650 --> 00:17:08.350
They came for a fight because they're confident!

00:17:08.800 --> 00:17:11.520
<i>I'm counting on you, Shigeno! Please do something!</i>

00:17:14.100 --> 00:17:17.210
<i>All right. We don't need any more strikes.</i>

00:17:18.080 --> 00:17:22.880
<i>If it's Honda-kun now, even if we miss with two or three balls, he'll try to swing.</i>

00:17:24.290 --> 00:17:26.810
<i>Let's bring his body up first with it high and inside,</i>

00:17:26.810 --> 00:17:27.410
<i>and after that...</i>

00:17:27.930 --> 00:17:29.250
<i>a breaking ball outside!</i>

00:18:02.110 --> 00:18:03.630
We did it!

00:18:03.630 --> 00:18:05.100
We're tied!

00:18:05.100 --> 00:18:06.450
A-Amazing!

00:18:19.960 --> 00:18:20.770
I-I'm sorry...

00:18:20.770 --> 00:18:21.750
I-I'm sorry...

00:18:22.430 --> 00:18:25.240
For him to hit it high and inside when we weren't even planning on letting him hit it,

00:18:25.240 --> 00:18:27.040
I hadn't even thought of that.

00:18:27.040 --> 00:18:29.360
I was wary of Honda-kun, 

00:18:29.360 --> 00:18:32.260
but I might have been the one who underestimated him the most. 

00:18:34.860 --> 00:18:36.730
It's not your fault.

00:18:37.970 --> 00:18:43.280
I underestimated Honda as well and thought too much of my skills.

00:18:43.280 --> 00:18:48.280
Just as you said, I shouldn't have tried to go up against a monster like him.

00:18:49.470 --> 00:18:50.950
Because of my selfishness...

00:18:51.520 --> 00:18:52.820
I'm sorry, everyone.

00:18:53.520 --> 00:18:55.540
What are you saying!?

00:18:56.180 --> 00:18:59.130
You guys went up against him because you didn't want to regret anything, right?

00:18:59.130 --> 00:19:04.580
If that's so, you shouldn't be apologizing to everyone when you regret it after getting hit!

00:19:04.580 --> 00:19:06.800
That's rude to everyone!

00:19:07.830 --> 00:19:09.050
Oobayashi...

00:19:11.600 --> 00:19:15.470
It's only tied, isn't it? Now's not the time to be depressed!

00:19:15.470 --> 00:19:18.640
That's right, we've only returned to the beginning!

00:19:19.010 --> 00:19:21.270
Yeah, we just have to score runs again.

00:19:23.630 --> 00:19:24.730
Yeah!

00:19:34.530 --> 00:19:35.700
Out!

00:19:35.700 --> 00:19:37.490
Three outs! Change!

00:19:38.230 --> 00:19:41.270
All right, the game's tied! Let's keep it going!

00:19:41.270 --> 00:19:41.960
YEAH!

00:19:43.550 --> 00:19:44.960
Are you all right, Taiga?

00:19:46.170 --> 00:19:47.380
What are you talking about?

00:19:47.380 --> 00:19:49.510
Not, "what are you talking about?"

00:19:49.510 --> 00:19:51.400
It's finally tied.

00:19:51.400 --> 00:19:54.640
If you're at your limit, then I have to go.

00:19:55.580 --> 00:19:58.740
That's cunning. Trying to take the good parts for yourself?

00:19:58.740 --> 00:19:59.820
What?

00:19:59.820 --> 00:20:01.650
Don't worry about it.

00:20:01.650 --> 00:20:05.110
This inning starts with the garbage hitters, so I'll do what I can.

00:20:05.560 --> 00:20:07.030
I see.

00:20:07.030 --> 00:20:09.600
But next time, if the situation turns bad, we're switching.

00:20:09.600 --> 00:20:12.600
If they hit a home run, we can't do anything, so be careful.

00:20:13.570 --> 00:20:16.740
Batting eighth: center fielder, Haraguchi-kun.

00:20:17.440 --> 00:20:18.320
Play!

00:20:18.700 --> 00:20:24.840
<i>We're only tied. I can't allow senpai, who can only throw 30 pitches, to get up on the mound.</i>

00:20:24.840 --> 00:20:28.380
<i>Until we're winning, I have to do my best!</i>

00:20:31.660 --> 00:20:32.220
Out!

00:20:32.660 --> 00:20:33.840
Nice, Fuji!

00:20:34.820 --> 00:20:37.940
Batting ninth: left fielder, Iwata-kun.

00:20:47.730 --> 00:20:48.750
Out!

00:20:48.750 --> 00:20:50.120
Nice, left!

00:20:50.120 --> 00:20:51.400
Two down! Two down!

00:20:51.940 --> 00:20:55.210
Batting first: shortstop, Nakayama-kun.

00:20:56.330 --> 00:20:59.120
After tying it up, the opponent's movements have gotten better...

00:20:59.120 --> 00:21:03.710
No, but now it's only a matter of time, Coach.

00:21:04.410 --> 00:21:08.670
That pitcher's speed and control is obviously getting worse.

00:21:09.370 --> 00:21:11.380
In the next inning... for sure.

00:21:13.780 --> 00:21:14.840
Dead ball!

00:21:15.450 --> 00:21:18.760
Batting second: second baseman, Ihara-kun.

00:21:19.850 --> 00:21:21.100
Damn!

00:21:22.560 --> 00:21:25.270
All right! Runners on first and second!

00:21:26.280 --> 00:21:28.480
Our chance has come sooner than expected, hasn't it?

00:21:28.920 --> 00:21:31.650
Batting third: first baseman, Oobayashi-kun.

00:21:34.750 --> 00:21:35.650
Do your best, Taiga!

00:21:36.180 --> 00:21:37.320
<i>Taiga!</i>

00:21:38.920 --> 00:21:44.410
<i>Damn, senpai is playing because he had freezing injected.</i>

00:21:44.410 --> 00:21:51.090
<i>Even if he says 30 pitches, he should've already put a lot of pressure on his right foot with all that hitting and running.</i>

00:21:51.670 --> 00:21:57.100
<i>He finally got back the four runs I let them have...</i>

00:21:57.920 --> 00:22:02.810
<i>I can't allow my senpai to cover for my mistakes anymore!</i>

00:22:22.930 --> 00:22:24.290
Safe! Safe!

00:22:24.650 --> 00:22:27.240
All right! The bases are loaded!

00:22:28.030 --> 00:22:29.280
Taiga!

00:22:28.820 --> 00:22:30.250
Taiga!

00:22:36.100 --> 00:22:38.130
I'm sorry, senpai.

00:22:38.980 --> 00:22:42.200
I can... even though I can still pitch...

00:22:42.200 --> 00:22:46.350
if I stay on the mound any longer, I'll be bothering everyone else.

00:22:48.000 --> 00:22:49.230
I'll leave the rest... to you.

00:22:49.230 --> 00:22:50.810
I'll leave the rest... to you.

00:22:53.000 --> 00:22:54.520
You did your best, Taiga.

00:22:55.630 --> 00:22:57.230
Don't worry.

00:22:57.230 --> 00:23:00.240
No matter how many innings we go, I'll throw the rest.

00:23:00.700 --> 00:23:02.200
Shigeno!

00:24:40.450 --> 00:24:42.720
Bottom of the eighth, two outs, and the bases are loaded.

00:24:42.720 --> 00:24:47.300
The result of the game depends on the battle with the fourth batter, Komori, huh?

00:24:47.300 --> 00:24:48.890
It's time for a battle, Komori.

00:24:48.890 --> 00:24:52.270
After beating you, I'm going to challenge Kaido! 

00:24:52.640 --> 00:24:54.100
Next time, Major:

00:24:54.100 --> 00:24:54.900
Full Swing!

00:24:55.530 --> 00:24:57.760
Run to the stage of your dreams!
